# Finding — Adversarial campaign record

> **Use.** This template records one adversarial finding as part of a
> campaign run. Findings flow through the 17-state lifecycle of
> `ADVERSARIAL_ASSURANCE_GOVERNANCE.md` §2. The `history[]` field is
> externalized (ADVR-18, M1) to keep individual finding records bounded.

## Frontmatter

```yaml
---
finding_id: "<stable-id, e.g. FIND-2026-07-28-001>"
campaign_ref: "<run_id of parent campaign>"
level: "A0|A1|A2"
severity: "S0|S1|S2|S3"
confidence: "CONFIRMED|PLAUSIBLE|REFUTED"
state: "<one of the 17 lifecycle states>"
discovered_by: "<agent or human identifier>"
discovered_at: "ISO8601 UTC"
surface: "<file path or system component>"
attack_class: "<e.g. prompt-injection|auth-bypass|schema-drift>"
---
```

## Required fields

| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | string | yes | stable across the campaign |
| `summary` | string | yes | ≤ 200 chars |
| `severity` | enum | yes | S0..S3 |
| `confidence` | enum | yes | CONFIRMED only blocks |
| `state` | enum | yes | per lifecycle |
| `reproduction` | string | yes | steps + expected + observed |
| `oracle` | string | yes | what the test asserts |
| `fails_before` | bool | when CONFIRMED | true (test reproduces) |
| `passes_after` | bool | when CONFIRMED | true (after fix) |

## Optional fields

| Field | Type | Required when | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `non_regression_lock.witnessed_by` | string | A2 CONFIRMED | distinct from `discovered_by` |
| `non_regression_lock.test_review` | string | A2 CONFIRMED | PASS\|FAIL by 2nd agent or human |
| `non_regression_lock.reviewed_by` | string | A1 within 30 days | 2nd agent review |
| `accepted_risk.owner` | string | ACCEPTED_RISK | human approver |
| `accepted_risk.expiry` | ISO8601 | ACCEPTED_RISK | deadline |
| `accepted_risk.reopen_trigger` | string | ACCEPTED_RISK | what reopens the finding |
| `history[]` | array | (externalized) | see `ADVERSARIAL_CAMPAIGN.md.template §history` |

## Promotion block (mandatory for CONFIRMED findings)

Per `ADVERSARIAL_ASSURANCE_GOVERNANCE.md` §9, every CONFIRMED finding
must answer all six destinations:

```yaml
promotion:
  destination_1_canonical_test: "tests/test_<id>.py"        # or "NOT_APPLICABLE: <reason>"
  destination_2_integration_test: "tests/integration/<id>.py" # or "NOT_APPLICABLE: <reason>"
  destination_3_certification_gate: "<new gate_id or vbb-*.py check>" # or "NOT_APPLICABLE: <reason>"
  destination_4_checklist: "<pre-merge|closeout|review item>" # or "NOT_APPLICABLE: <reason>"
  destination_5_normative_rule: "candidate_id=<id>  # routes via ADR 0049 OBSERVATION→CANONICAL"
  destination_6_adversarial_corpus: "<corpus entry id or path>" # MANDATORY, never NOT_APPLICABLE
```

## Reproduction format

```yaml
reproduction:
  setup: "<commands or context to reproduce>"
  steps:
    - "<step 1>"
    - "<step 2>"
  expected: "<expected behavior>"
  observed: "<observed behavior>"
  oracle: "<what the test asserts>"
```

## Non-regression lock

```yaml
non_regression_lock:
  test_id: "<test identifier>"
  test_path: "<path to test file>"
  fails_before: true
  passes_after: true
  # A2 only
  witnessed_by: "<distinct identifier>"
  test_review: "PASS|FAIL"
  test_review_reviewer: "<agent or human>"
```

## History (externalized)

The full history of state transitions is stored in the parent
campaign record, not in this finding. The finding carries only the
*current* state and the *origin* transition. The campaign record
holds the complete `history[]` for traceability.

## Notes

- A finding can only have one `state` at a time.
- `REFUTED` findings are kept (negative evidence prevents re-litigation).
- The promotion block is mandatory at `state ∈ {REMEDIATED,
  NON_REGRESSION_LOCKED, CLOSED_REMEDIATED, CLOSED_ACCEPTED,
  CLOSED_REJECTED}`.